{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Therefore whoever slays.</b> The reason for ״לָכֵן״ is that he recognized and knew that if HaShem did not guard him, whoever found him would kill him; because of this mitzvah HaShem had compassion upon him and said ״כָּל הוֹרֵג״ etc. And HaShem inscribed a sign on his face, after the manner practiced regarding one who performs a mitzvah, that a sign is inscribed on his forehead for good. This is what the verse says: <b>and HaShem set a sign for Cain</b>. And it is along the lines of what they of blessed memory expounded (Shemot Rabbah, chapter 16) on the verse ״וְהָיָה הַדָּם לָכֶם לְאוֹת״ (Exodus 12:13) — meaning, a sign of mitzvah for them, for protection."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The Hebrew citation reads 'שמות רבה פרק י״ז' (chapter 17), but the referenced drash on Exodus 12:13 appears in Shemot Rabbah chapter 16; the citation has been rendered as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:39:18.895108300Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}